<p style="border:none;padding:0.0in"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><em><b><span style="font-size:9.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black">For additional benefit information available to State of Florida employees, go to </span></span></span></span></b></em><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.mybenefits.myflorida.com%2F&amp;data=04%7C01%7CLisa.Hill%40dot.state.fl.us%7C1b05f6cc78404168722108d9f86420cb%7Cdb21de5dbc9c420c8f3f8f08f85b5ada%7C0%7C0%7C637813931195761858%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&amp;sdata=3POI7SRd37PUUZjr%2BSFguwDJAZD%2FEhRwtT9rYeyz2PY%3D&amp;reserved=0" style="color:blue;text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-size:9.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">https://www.mybenefits.myflorida.com/</span></span></span></a></span></span></span></p>
</div>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS:</span></span></span></b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">  You may be required to provide your Social Security Number to conduct required verifications. Male applicants born on or after October 1, 1962, will not be eligible for hire or promotion in the Career Service, or appointment in the Selected Exempt Service (SES) or Senior Management Service (SMS) unless they are registered with the Selective Service System (SSS) before their 26th birthday, or have a Letter of Registration Exemption from the SSS.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">THE FLORIDA DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION VALUES AND SUPPORTS EMPLOYMENT OF INDIVIDUALS WITH DISABILITIES.  QUALIFIED INDIVIDUALS WITH DISABILITIES ARE ENCOURAGED TO APPLY. </span></span></span></b><br>
<span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">In accordance with Section 110.112, Florida Statutes, and the Florida Department of Transportation’s Individuals with Disabilities Affirmative Action Plan, the agency is committed to ensuring affirmative action and equal employment opportunity for qualified individuals with disabilities.  Upon request and as appropriate, reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities may be provided.  Please contact the Florida Department of Transportation’s Human Resources Office located at 605 Suwannee Street, Tallahassee, Florida 32399, or call (850) 414-5300 for assistance.   </span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="vertical-align:baseline"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black">This position requires a valid Class (E) driver license with an acceptable driving record in accordance with the Department's Drivers Record Requirements Policy. An unacceptable driving record is defined as any of the following:</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<ol style="margin-top:16.0px">
	<li><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span><span style="vertical-align:baseline"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span>three (3) or more moving violations in the past 3 years that accumulate 3 or more points per violation;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
	<li><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span><span style="vertical-align:baseline"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span>any 2 convictions of reckless driving in the past 3 years;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
	<li><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span><span style="vertical-align:baseline"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span>a suspension or revocation of the driver license for moving violations in the past 3 years; and</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
	<li><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span><span style="vertical-align:baseline"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span>a suspension or revocation for refusal to take a sobriety test, or any suspension or revocation for a DUI conviction </span></span></span></span><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span>in the past 4 years</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
</ol>

<p> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span>Your driving record will be reviewed and the status of your driver license confirmed.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">POSITION DESCRIPTION: </span></span></span></b></span></span></span><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">Performs and serves as a Construction Manager for the South Miami-Dade Construction Residency in support of highway and bridge construction program. Supervises employees by communicating regularly, plans, organizes, coordinates and schedules assigned work for employees. Motivates, trains and evaluates employees on the performance of their duties. Supervises subordinates administering consultant and construction contracts, final estimates preparation, and materials coordination. Ensures all work is completed in compliance with the established procedures for each discipline. Advises staff with regards to all aspects of Florida Department of Transportation (FDOT) construction contract administration matters. Participates in applicant selection and hiring process. Provides employee orientation, training, counseling and disciplinary actions, and prepares employee performance evaluations.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">Oversees project administration by monitoring the activities of contractors and subcontractors to ensure compliance with the contract documents. Monitors field related project issues and provides guidance to project staff in handling construction engineering problems effectively and timely. Assists Resident Engineer in administration of the construction office by reviewing, analyzing and making decisions or recommendations on contract and engineering specification interpretation, scope and intent of contracts, time extensions, supplemental agreements and claims or disputes. Ensures proper preparation and timely submittal of project documentation by the Project Administrator (Monthly Estimate, Supplemental Agreements, Monthly Status Reports, Contractor's rating, etc.). This position will make field reviews and inspections. This position will sign and seal engineering documents.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">Oversees the administration and scheduling of project staff on all general assignment and hybrid construction contracts needed on in-house projects. Ensures project staff properly administer all contract work for compliance with contract documents. Attends pre-construction conference meetings. Participates in the review and selection of Consultant Construction Engineering and Inspection firms. Participates in the contract negotiation with selected Consultant Construction Engineering and Inspection firms. Participates in semi-final and final inspections on completed construction projects to minimize problem areas. Oversees the on-the-job field interviews for coordinating requirements for Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO), Labor Law Compliance and On Job Training (OJT) compliance programs with the Resident Compliance Specialist.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">Interprets all plans and specifications for Resident Office as it relates to Construction Contract Administration. Analyzes, documents, and negotiates contract changes and claims. Oversees the processing of Supplemental Agreements, Work Orders, Change Orders, Time Extensions, and Time Suspensions to ensure they are accurate and completed in a timely manner. Ensures daily work reports and diaries are prepared in SiteManager, as required. Prepares correspondence as necessary to document project conditions. Ensures that monthly documentation (Status Report, Weather Letter, Contractor's Past Performance, etc.) are prepared as required. Ensures project files are maintained in accordance with Department requirements. Reviews and prepares response to contractor's request for changes to the contract documents.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">Performs Consultant Construction Engineering and Inspection (CCEI) contract administration. Develops manpower estimates, scope of services, technical questions and other necessary materials for consultant selection. Reviews and recommends approval of monthly invoices and personnel action requests within the required timeframes. Performs quarterly CCEI evaluations and completed final CCEI rating within 30 days of completion of CEI services.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">Reviews plans and specifications for future projects In Residency; coordinates and assigns Design Phase Reviews. Reviews and comments in writing on Department's procedures and specifications. Visits project sites and makes field reviews.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">Conducts public relations activities by resolving conflicts/issues with citizens who are affected by</span></span></span></span></span></span><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"> projects under the Department's jurisdiction. Discusses projects with various groups and business representatives. Notifies the public of upcoming construction activities, as well as, providing status reports during the life of the project as required.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">Oversees contract-related activities such as testing of materials, methods of construction and measurement of quantities. Oversees preparation of the Final Estimate Package for each assigned project and ensures the Final Estimate is prepared in compliance with the Basis of Estimates Manual, Construction Project Administration Manual, Field Standards for Final Estimates Manual, contract specifications and other related documents. Oversees Electronic Document Management System (EDMS) activities</span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black">KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: </span></span></span></b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Knowledge of the concepts, terminology, principles of road and bridge construction and maintenance; Knowledge of engineering design, construction, production and/or operations; Skilled in contract administration and related activities between the department and contractor; Ability to determine work priorities, assign work, and ensure proper completion of work assignments; Ability to implement programs necessary to achieve objectives; Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships; Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing; Ability to supervise people; Ability to direct, monitor and inspect engineering projects; Skilled in using computer software applications; Knowledge of Construction Project Administration Manual; Knowledge of conflict resolution and negotiating techniques; Skilled in utilizing problem solving techniques; Ability to analyze and interpret engineering data.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black">REQUIRED LICENSURE/REGISTRATION/CERTIFICATION: </span></span></span></b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Registration as a professional engineer in accordance with chapter 471, Florida Statutes.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="text-align:justify"> </p>

<p style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">OTHER JOB RELATED REQUIREMENTS: </span></span></b><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;, sans-serif">During a declared emergency event, the incumbent will be required to assist the district as needed. Responsible for adhering to the provisions and requirements of section 215.422, F.S. related to State comptroller's rules and department of transportation's invoice processing and warrant distribution procedures. During a declared emergency event, the incumbent may be required to drive a state owned or leased vehicle to perform the duties of this position. A valid class "E" driver's license is required. This position may be required to work extraordinary hours, including nights/weekends.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>The State of Florida is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Affirmative Action Employer, and does not tolerate discrimination or violence in the workplace.</p>

<p>Candidates requiring a reasonable accommodation, as defined by the Americans with Disabilities Act, must notify the agency hiring authority and/or People First Service Center (1-866-663-4735). Notification to the hiring authority must be made in advance to allow sufficient time to provide the accommodation.</p>

<p>The State of Florida supports a Drug-Free workplace. All employees are subject to reasonable suspicion drug testing in accordance with Section 112.0455, F.S., Drug-Free Workplace Act.</p>
                </span>
    </span>
